# tally 2.1.8 §4 (#162), L §8.4 Load refuses what load sees: flat's price px is keyed by the index ks, which holds
# neither flat nor PLN: LOAD-KEY at load, whatever the asks read, as for a price keyed by a kind (tally 2.1.7 R5).
# 2.1.7's refcore loaded it clean (RUN-KEY where value read it).
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-06-30
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
index ks = [a, b]
kind homes: place PLN min 0 priced px
place flat: homes lives 2026-01-01..
input px[k in ks]: num PLN
input n: int

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  n = 1 "s"

ask q: n
=== expect
refused: LOAD-KEY flat is priced by px, keyed by ks, which holds neither flat nor its unit (m.tally:10)
